linenoise from https://github.com/antirez/linenoise
commit a473823d74b93eab2ba83480df16ed37617493f2 (2026-05-01).
Built through ../lua_all.c (not compiled on its own).

Patched so it works on any fds (the Lua console PTY), never on the app's stdin/stdout:
- enableRawMode: isatty(fd) instead of isatty(STDIN_FILENO)
- getColumns: ioctl(ofd, ...) instead of ioctl(1, ...); 80 columns when unknown
  (no ESC[6n query: the console emulator may not answer it, and the read would block)
- linenoiseClearScreen: write(rawmode_output, ...) instead of STDOUT_FILENO
- linenoiseEditStop: write(l->ofd, "\n") instead of printf
- raw mode on/off with TCSADRAIN instead of TCSAFLUSH, so typed-ahead or pasted lines
  are not dropped
